      en: "The oldest house in Cuba still standing, built for the Spanish conqueror. Built around 1515. Shows Moorish style elements. Served as residence and trading house. Thus, the site is among the characteristic points of Cuba, the Caribbean island nation, reflecting the interplay of history, tobacco and sugarcane cultivation, and tropical nature. Located in Cuba, the largest island state in the Caribbean. Tropical-humid climate with distinct wet and dry seasons. Havana, the capital, is the country's political and cultural hub."
